    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-8939-1",
        "name": "USN-8939-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain RECORD replies from the X server. A malicious X server could possibly use this issue to cause libXtst clients to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-94286)  Tobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain memory operations. A malicious X server could possibly use this issue to cause libXtst to access memory out of bounds, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-7951)  Tobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain replies from the X server. A malicious X server could possibly use this issue to cause libXtst to enter an infinite loop, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS. (CVE-2016-7952)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2016-7951",
          "CVE-2016-7952",
          "CVE-2026-94286"
        ]
      },
